Job Description:
The Family & Early Childhood (FEC) division sits under the Family and Child Development (FCD) Policy Directorate. The FEC division formulates and reviews policies that promote and strengthen families, in support of MSF’s macro outcomes to support marriage and parenthood actualisation and build strong and resilient marriages and families.  •	Strong analytical and critical thinking, writing and communication skills
•	Ability to analyse issues from a strategic perspective and take a system view, while having a good grasp of details and processes
•	Strong problem-solving skills
•	Good stakeholder engagement and management skills 
•	Candidates with relevant working experience would have an advantage
•	Ability to work well independently and in teams
•	Driven and proactive, able to lead projects independently

Only shortlisted candidates will be notified within 4 weeks from the closing date of this position. The officer will work with other stakeholders in the Government to formulate and review policies. 

•	Study emerging trends and assess its impact on families; 
•	Understand Singaporeans’ attitudes and beliefs about the institution of family;
•	Develop and execute engagement plans with community stakeholders to build networks and trust, and gain a better understanding of different views towards the institution of family; 
•	Continually assess and shape the definition and perception of family in Singapore, while accounting for demographic trends and evolving social norms; 
•	Conduct robust research and analysis, and engage stakeholders to understand and strengthen the ecosystem of family support services and programmes;
•	Formulate effective policies and programmes, with other agencies to address potential gaps that support various types of families; and 
•	Review legislation to ensure it remains relevant in supporting our policies and programmes.

You will be involved in reviewing and refining existing programmes and services, engage and collaborate with stakeholders across various sectors to understand the needs/ gaps and drive the co-solutioning and co-delivery of solutions, secure resources needed to deliver more comprehensive and holistic support, and enhance accessibility for persons with disabilities so that they can achieve their potential and actively participate in society. •	Preferable 5 years of working experience in public service with experience in policy formulations and reviews;
•	Possess good written and communication skills;
•	Ability to engage and build relations with carious stakeholders;
•	Detail oriented;
•	Diligent, resourceful and able to multi-task in a dynamic work environment;
•	Team player, and exercise initiative at work; and
•	Effective time management and good organisation skills, able to manage tight timelines and deliver outcomes in a fast-paced working environment.

You will be notified whether you have been shortlisted within 4 weeks from the closing date of this job posting. 
 •	Overseeing the corporate and governance-related issues for SG Enable;
•	Formulate, review and implement policies and initiatives in areas such as assistive technology, accessibility etc to serve the needs of persons with disabilities; and
•	Work with stakeholders across government agencies and SG Enable to co-develop solutions and implement initiatives.
•	Lead a small team.

This is an individual contributor role in the Resourcing and Ecosystem (RE) Division of the Ministry of Social and Family Development (MSF).

RE aims to cultivate a future-ready social service sector that delivers quality services, is well-resourced, and has high levels of community engagement and contribution. As a team, we value and uphold critical systems-thinking, initiative and accountability, effective verbal and written communication, and collaboration with key stakeholders. We are looking for individuals who share these attributes.

Prior experience and a strong interest in public policy, social impact, technology and/or digital adoption would be advantageous. You will develop and implement strategies, policies, and projects to empower Singapore’s social service sector to have a greater positive impact. For example, you will:

• Govern and administer funding to the social service sector;
• Develop a strategy and implementation plan on how to incentivise and support greater impact measurement and evaluation in the social service sector;
• Develop a strategy and implementation plan on how to incentivise and support more intentional and outcome-oriented technology adoption within the social service sector;
• Evaluate the latest philanthropic giving and social impact investing models and trends, and develop ways for the social service sector to better leverage such systems; and/or
• Develop and maintain strategic partnerships with other social service stakeholders to develop the social service sector.
